WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
Organizations do not necessarily implement every control in the catalog.

2
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:16.124
NIST supports a risk-based approach that allows organizations to select and tailor controls based on mission needs, regulatory requirements, system impact, and risk tolerance.

3
00:00:16.124 --> 00:00:18.738
Control baselines provide starting points.

4
00:00:18.738 --> 00:00:25.343
A baseline can help teams avoid beginning with an empty page when deciding which safeguards may apply to a system.

5
00:00:25.343 --> 00:00:28.796
Tailoring adjusts the starting point to fit the actual environment.

6
00:00:28.796 --> 00:00:40.440
Organizations may add controls, refine parameters, document exceptions, or apply overlays based on mission, threat, law, policy, and system characteristics.

7
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.057
Good tailoring is accountable.

8
00:00:42.057 --> 00:00:48.552
Decisions should be documented, justified, and connected to risk rather than treated as informal preference.
